 "callout": "<b>Why this sits alongside the GA4 dashboard.</b> Hong Kong's GA4 bookings are up <b>12.3% YoY</b>, and covers tell you what that demand is actually worth and where it comes from. GA4 only fires for bookings made on our own website, so it never sees <b>OpenRice</b> (about a sixth of Hong Kong covers this week), only partly captures <b>Google Reserve</b>, and is completely blind to walk-ins and the reception desks, which between them are close to <b>six tenths of all covers</b>. Read the two together: GA4 is the scoreboard for the channel we control and can optimise, covers are the full demand picture. One caveat on this week's record 13,191 covers: roughly 850 of them come from two one-off private events booked through reception (a 600-cover booking at Aqua Hong Kong and a 250-cover booking at The Chinese Library), so the underlying run rate is closer to 12,300.",
